{ The two rooks are yours this time, and his king is all alone against the edge column. One move finishes him with a ladder mate. } 1... Ra2# { Mate! One rook checks along the edge column and the other seals the column beside it, so every square round his king is covered. [%csl Gb1,Ra4] } (1... Rc4+ { A check along the row, but nothing of yours covers the rows beside him, so his king just steps to the next one and lives a move longer. } 2. Ka3 Rb7 3. Ka2 { Your rooks are lined up again and the mate is one move away, but that stray check gave his king a free step. }) (1... Rb4+ { His king is standing right next to that square, and no rook of yours defends it there. He takes, and your ladder loses a rung. } 2. Kxb4 Kg2 3. Kb5 Kf3 { A whole rook gone for nothing. A single rook can still mate, but you will be chasing his king for a very long time. }) (1... Ra1+ { Your rook leaves the column beside him to give this check, so his king simply walks through the gap and out into open space. } 2. Kb3 Rac1 3. Kb4 Rb1+ { Your rooks are still winning, but his king has escaped the edge and you have to walk him all the way back again. }) 0-1


