{ His king is stuck against the edge of the board and your king is standing right across from him. One move ends the game. } 1. Qh2# { Mate! Your queen seals the whole column his king stands on, and your king holds the three squares beside him. That is the king and queen mate. [%csl Gf5,Rh5] } (1. Qh4+ { Your queen steps right beside his king, but your own king is too far away to guard her there. } 1... Kxh4 { He simply takes her off the board, and a bare king can never mate anybody. It is a draw. [%csl Rh4] }) (1. Qf4 { His king has no square to go to and he is not in check, so it is stalemate: a draw, out of a position you were winning easily. }) (1. Qf3+ { A check along the diagonal, but it hands his king a free square away from the edge, so he escapes the box. } 1... Kh6 2. Qb7 Kh5 3. Qh1# { Mate three moves later. Your queen seals the column once more and your king takes the squares beside his king. }) (1. Qe2+ { Another check from far away. He steps off the edge, and now you have to walk him back there all over again. } 1... Kh6 2. Qe7 Kh5 3. Qg5# { Mate at the third try. Your queen stands next to his king and your king holds her there, so he cannot take her. }) 1-0


